# Project Documentation Phase - Implement Client Script & UI Policy for Incident

## 1. Project Overview
This project implements Client Scripts and UI Policies in ServiceNow to enhance Incident form functionality, improve user experience, and ensure data quality.

## 2. Tools & Technologies Used
- ServiceNow PDI (Rome/Utah version)
- Incident Table
- Client Scripts (onLoad, onChange, onSubmit)
- UI Policy & UI Policy Actions
- GitHub for Documentation

## 3. Implementation Summary
- Created 3 Client Scripts for validation and alerts
- Created 2 UI Policies for dynamic field visibility
- Configured conditions based on Category and Priority fields
- Tested in multiple scenarios

## 4. Key Learnings
- Understood difference between Client Script and UI Policy
- Learned g_form API methods: getValue(), setMandatory(), setVisible(), addInfoMessage()
- Learned execution order and best practices

## 5. Screenshots / Evidence
- Client Script configuration screenshots
- UI Policy configuration screenshots
- Incident form before and after implementation

## 6. Final Deliverables
- All required files documented in GitHub
- ServiceNow PDI with working Client Scripts and UI Policies
- Project Report ready for submission

## 7. Conclusion
Successfully implemented Client Script and UI Policy for Incident table. This improves form behavior and ensures mandatory data entry for critical incidents.

